{
  "name": "session-end",
  "description": "What OpenCode's `session.deleted` lowers to: a SessionEvent with action end, carrying the TERMINAL boundary — the session is over, nothing more is coming. It is the only ONE-SHOT end signal OpenCode offers (`session.idle` fires once per assistant turn and is deliberately not mapped, or every turn would look like an ending). The marker is byte-identical to the one Claude Code's `SessionEnd` produces: a consumer switches on `boundary`, not on which agent it came from (issue #169).",
